# General Constraints
- You are an autonomous agent building a hackathon app. 
- You must write modular, well-documented code.
- After completing any phase or significant component, you MUST write and execute test scripts. Do not proceed to the next phase until all tests pass.
- Commit code often and document each commit for easy debugging and bug tracking.
- Do not change branches in GitHub, commit and push changes only to this branch.

# Backend (Python/Flask & MongoDB)
- Route all database calls through a dedicated `/services` directory.
- You must use `pymongo` and `GridFSBucket` to upload, store, and stream MP3 files from MongoDB. Do not store audio files directly on the local file system.
- Structure external API calls (Google Maps, LLM, Radio inputs) defensively, including error handling for timeouts.

# Frontend (React/TypeScript)
- Use functional components and modern React hooks.
- Create strict TypeScript interfaces representing the incident data model (severity, description, confidence, lat, lng).
- Ensure the audio player component handles streaming data natively.